```text
1. Frontend rework: introduce Request envelope, shift exchange to item-mutation pattern
    [x] 'content/core/engine_deps/result.py': Add Request dataclass; update FrontendService port signatures
        - Add `Request` dataclass with `id: str` and `item: Command | Result`
        - Change `FrontendService.get_request()` return type from `Command` to `Request`
        - Change `FrontendService.post_response()` param from `result: Result` to `req: Request`
    [x] 'content/core/engine.py': Rewrite run() loop around Request mutation
        - `req = self.frontend.get_request()` (no more `item is None` sentinel)
        - `match req.item:` — each case mutates `req.item = <new Command or Result>`
        - `if isinstance(req.item, Result): self.frontend.post_response(req)`
        - `case ExitCommand(): break` stays; final return is `req.item.exit_msg`
        - Remove the old `item = None` reset and the separate `item` variable entirely
    [x] 'content/modules/tui/tui_service.py': Mint Request in frontend, pass Request to post_response
        - `__init__`: queue a `Request(id=..., item=BootCmd())` instead of bare `BootCmd()`
        - `get_request()` → `return self.renderer.read_request()` (now returns `Request`)
        - `post_response(req: Request)`: match on `req.item` instead of a bare `Result` arg
        - Internal queue type: `Queue[Request]`
    [x] 'content/modules/tui/renderer.py': TUIRenderer mints Request on char-read and on queue-put
        - `TUIRenderer.queue` type: `Queue[Command]` → `Queue[Request]`
        - `read_request()`: queue-empty path → mint `Request(id=..., item=KbCmd(char=...))`; abort path → `Request(id=..., item=UserAborted())`; queue-hit path → return `queue.get()` directly (already a `Request`)
        - `post_question(...)`: mint `Request(id=..., item=cmd)` before `self.queue.put(...)` (applies to both StartCmd and ClankerizeCmd branches)
        - `get_acknowledgement(...)`: mint `Request(id=..., item=exit_cmd())` before `self.queue.put(...)`
        - `display_result(result: KbServiceEmission)` signature unchanged — caller in tui_service passes `req.item`
    [x] 'content/modules/web_frontend/web_frontend_service.py': Mint Request in _handle_char, key _pending on request.id
        - `__init__`: queue a `Request(id=..., item=BootCmd())`
        - `_handle_char()`: mint `Request(id=..., item=KbCmd(char=char_val))`; store `self._pending[request.id] = slot`; `self._queue.put(request)`
        - `get_request()`: `return self._queue.get()` (pops a `Request`)
        - `post_response(req: Request)`: match on `req.item`; resolve slot via `self._pending.pop(req.id, None)` in both the `PromptRenderResult` and `_` branches
        - `_pending` type: `dict[str, _ReplySlot]` (key is `request.id`, not `id(cmd)`)
        - Prohibition: do not retain the old `id(cmd)` / `id(result.cmd.cmd)` keying pattern
